## How to read this changelog

- **Added**: new sources, new columns, new concepts.
- **Changed**: behavior changes that don't affect output rows or
  schema.
- **Deprecated**: features that still work but will be removed.
- **Removed**: features no longer in the pipeline.
- **Fixed**: bug fixes that change output values. **These are the
  entries to read carefully if you've already cited a number from this
  dataset.**
- **Schema migrations**: changes to the canonical column list or
  unit of observation. The most disruptive category; pay closest
  attention here.

When a fix changes a previously-cited number, the entry will note that
explicitly and link to the affected commit.
